body:
**Feature request 🙏**
I would like to be able to pass an object of template variables into custom templates so I don't need to write custom render functions for widgets

Something that would look like this:

```
refinementList({
  container: '.container',
  templates: {
    item: myItemTemplate,
    templateData: {
      foo: 'bar'
    }
  }
});
```

Where `foo` is exposed for use inside the Handlebars template along with existing vars:

```
// myItemTemplate.hbs
<p>{{label}} ({{count}}) - {{ foo }}</p>
```

comments.body:
Hey @cloakedninjas – we don't get this request often but there's a workaround to pass custom attributes to your template using the [`transformItems`](https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/refinement-list/js/#widget-param-transformitems) option.

Here's an example:

```js
search.addWidget(
  instantsearch.widgets.refinementList({
    container: '#brand-list',
    attribute: 'brand',
    transformItems: items => items.map(item => ({
      ...item,
      customAttribute: 'whatever', // add your own attribute
    })),
    templates: {
      item: ({ label, customAttribute }) => `${label} – ${customAttribute}`,
    },
  })
);
```

Let me know if that works for you!
